# Cloudflare Workers Static Assets redirect rules.
#
# Format:  <from>  <to>  <status>      — one rule per line, whitespace-separated.
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# This file lives at the repo root because wrangler.jsonc sets assets.directory
# to "./". It is parsed by Workers and is NOT served as a public asset.
#
# IMPORTANT — redirects beat real files. Cloudflare: "Redirects are always
# followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming request."
# So a bad rule can shadow a live page. Always redirect FROM a path you have
# actually removed, and never point a rule at itself.
#
# Limits: 2,000 static rules, 100 dynamic (wildcard/placeholder), 2,100 total,
# 1,000 characters per line.

# --- ACTIVE RULES ------------------------------------------------------------
/fr/  /fr/salaire-net-quebec/  301

# Inbound links from retired satellite sites (older page template). These paths
# have never existed in this repo — grep confirms zero internal links to any of
# them, so these mask nothing. Search Console 404s, 2026-08-15.
#
# Extensionless bare paths (/about, /faq) are handled natively by
# assets.html_handling = "auto-trailing-slash" in wrangler.jsonc, not here.
# Listed below only where the target is NOT the trailing-slash version.
/privacy       /privacy-policy/  301
/privacy.html  /privacy-policy/  301
/legal         /disclaimer/      301
/legal.html    /disclaimer/      301
/terms         /disclaimer/      301
/terms.html    /disclaimer/      301
/faq           /faq/             301
/contact.html  /contact/         301
/about.html    /about/           301
#
# /methodology/<topic>/ is a PATTERN, not a fixed set. The retired satellites cite
# calc-hq.ca as their authority source at /methodology/ URLs that were never built
# here, so new variants keep surfacing. Enumerating them failed: the 2026-08-15 fix
# mapped only /methodology/ and /methodology/termination-pay/, and Google crawled
# /methodology/ontario-income-tax/ on 2026-08-18 — that 404 is what failed the
# Search Console validation. A wildcard catches the whole shape instead.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: _redirects matches top-down and the first hit wins, so the
# specific rule must stay ABOVE the wildcard or the wildcard swallows it and
# /methodology/termination-pay/ lands on /faq/ instead of the ESA page.
/methodology/termination-pay/  /employment-standards/esa-termination/  301
/methodology/*                 /faq/                                   301
/ontario-raise-calculator/     /payroll/pay-raise/                     301
#
# VERIFIED WORKING on this deploy 2026-07-18 (see MAINTENANCE.md):
#   - plain 301                 /from /to 301
#   - wildcard + :splat         /old/*  /new/:splat  301
#   - query strings are preserved through the redirect
#   - this file is not served publicly (a request for /_redirects returns 404)

# Trailing-slash normalisation, as explicit 301s.
#
# assets.html_handling does this natively but answers 307 (temporary), which
# does not consolidate the URL or pass link equity. These rules override it
# with a permanent 301. Enumerated rather than wildcarded: _redirects has no
# regex, and the only matching wildcard (/* -> /:splat/) would also rewrite
# /sitemap.xml and turn /about/ into /about//.
#
# MAINTENANCE: one line per page. Add a rule when you add a page.
# `node scripts/check-redirects.mjs` fails if a page is missing one, and also
# catches a rule that shadows a live page, loops, or chains into another rule.
